<h2>After the Emergency: Permanent Repairs</h2>
<p>Once the roof is secured, we come back in daylight for a full inspection. You get a photo report showing the damage, what caused it and what it will take to fix — whether that is a targeted <a href="/services/roof-repair/">roof repair</a>, storm repairs after <a href="/services/hail-damage-repair/">hail</a> or <a href="/services/wind-damage-repair/">wind damage</a>, or a full replacement if the roof was already near the end of its life. If you are unsure which way to go, our <a href="/roofing-tools/repair-or-replace-quiz/">repair or replace quiz</a> gives you a quick first read.</p>

<h2>Why Austin Sees So Many Roof Emergencies</h2>
<p>Central Texas weather turns quickly. Spring supercells bring hail and damaging straight-line winds, often in the late afternoon and evening. Summer is mostly dry and scorching, which bakes sealants and pipe boots until the first big downpour finds every crack. Tropical moisture can push heavy rain inland in late summer and fall, and Austin’s flash-flood-prone terrain is a reminder of how much water a single storm can drop in a short time.</p>
<p>Then there are the trees. Mature live oaks and pecans shade much of Austin, and limbs weakened by drought, heat or oak wilt can come down in winds that would otherwise do little harm. Keeping branches trimmed back from the roof is one of the cheapest forms of emergency prevention.</p>

<div class="callout callout--tip"><p><strong>Filing an insurance claim?</strong> Keep receipts for emergency tarping and any water cleanup. Our photo report documents the storm damage, and we can meet your adjuster at the property. See how we help on the <a href="/services/roof-insurance-claims/">roof insurance claim help</a> page.</p></div>

<h2>Emergency Service for Commercial and Multi-Family Properties</h2>
<p>When a roof fails over a store, office or apartment building, the clock runs faster. Water reaching inventory, equipment or occupied units multiplies the cost every hour. For property managers and business owners, our emergency crews focus on three things: stopping water entry at the source, protecting tenants and contents below, and documenting conditions for owners and insurers. On flat roofs that often means clearing clogged drains to relieve ponding, patching splits or punctures, and resecuring torn edge metal before the next band of rain arrives. Afterward, we provide a written plan for permanent repairs through our <a href="/services/commercial-roofing/">commercial roofing</a> or <a href="/services/multifamily-roofing/">multi-family roofing</a> teams.</p>

